                    <script id="json-data" type="application/json">
                [{"id":"the-banality-of-evil","s":"The Banality of Evil: Hannah Arendt, France, 1940  <p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">In May 1940, three German Jewish women are arrested in France \u2013 Hannah Arendt, who would become one of the 20th century&#8217;s most influential political theorists, the artist Charlotte Salomon, and the Communist schoolgirl Eva Daube.<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Branded \u201cUndesirables\u201d and transported to Camp Gurs, they find themselves among thousands of prisoners held by the state that once promised them refuge. As German forces advance, each woman must confront an impossible choice: stay and hope for liberation, or risk her life to escape into a dangerous and unknown future.<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Blending satire, physical theatre and cabaret, <\/span><i><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">The Banality of Evil <\/span><\/i><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">draws on archival research and testimony to reveal forgotten histories of women caught between exile, imprisonment and survival. At its centre is a pivotal moment in the life of 33 year-old Hannah Arendt that would later inform her writing on power and human rights.<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">A world premiere from writer and director Julia Pascal (<\/span><i><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Blueprint Medea<\/span><\/i><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">; <\/span><i><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Crossing Jerusalem<\/span><\/i><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">).<\/span><\/p>\n<h3>No latecomers, no readmittance.<\/h3>\n","dates":["2026-10-24","2026-10-24","2026-10-26","2026-10-27","2026-10-28","2026-10-29","2026-10-29","2026-10-30","2026-10-31","2026-10-31","2026-11-02","2026-11-03","2026-11-04","2026-11-05","2026-11-05","2026-11-06","2026-11-07","2026-11-07"],"date":"2026-10-24 15:00:00","daterange":{"start":"2026-10-08","end":"2026-11-07"},"type":[],"offer":[],"access":["captioned-performance","relaxed-performance"]},{"id":"the-master-builder","s":"The Master Builder  <p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Halvard Solness, a leading architect at the height of his fame, is paralysed by fear. Fear of the younger generation. Fear of irrelevance. Fear of the past catching up with him.<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">When young, enigmatic Hilde Wangel bursts back into his world, she reminds him of the promise he made her ten years ago.\u00a0<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">As she inspires him to even greater heights, Solness is forced to confront the true cost of his success. Will his final creation set him free, or be his downfall?<\/span><\/p>\n<p><strong>Greg Hicks<\/strong> stars, reuniting with Arcola\u2019s Artistic Director <strong>Mehmet Ergen<\/strong> following sold-out productions <em>An Enemy of The People<\/em> and <em>Richard III<\/em>, in this bold new staging of <strong>Henrik Ibsen\u2019s<\/strong> masterpiece about ambition and legacy.<\/p>\n","dates":["2026-10-24","2026-10-26","2026-10-27","2026-10-28","2026-10-29","2026-10-30","2026-10-31","2026-10-31","2026-11-02","2026-11-03","2026-11-04","2026-11-05","2026-11-06","2026-11-07","2026-11-07","2026-11-09","2026-11-10","2026-11-11","2026-11-12","2026-11-12","2026-11-13","2026-11-14","2026-11-14","2026-11-16","2026-11-17","2026-11-18","2026-11-19","2026-11-19","2026-11-20","2026-11-21","2026-11-21"],"date":"2026-10-24 19:00:00","daterange":{"start":"2026-10-16","end":"2026-11-21"},"type":[],"offer":[],"access":["captioned-performance","relaxed-performance"]},{"id":"squid-a-victim-impact-statement","s":"SQUID: A Victim Impact Statement  <p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">What if your life\u2019s work revealed secrets you didn\u2019t even know you had\u2026<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">For more than thirty years, writer and filmmaker Johnny Daukes unknowingly documented a story he could neither remember nor understand. Songs, scripts and films kept returning to the same themes, each becoming another fragment of an unwitting documentary, pointing towards a truth buried deep beneath memory.<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">As long-suppressed events began to surface, those creative works took on an extraordinary new significance, revealing not only Johnny\u2019s history of childhood abuse, but the mysterious ways in which his mind had protected itself.\u00a0<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Following an exhausting process that came to a conclusion at the Old Bailey earlier this year, <\/span><i><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">SQUID <\/span><\/i><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">explores how art and music can preserve what memory has buried \u2014 and ultimately help bring it back into the light.<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Blending live music, humour and storytelling, <\/span><i><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">SQUID: A Victim Impact Statement<\/span><\/i><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> is a true story about memory, creativity and an accidental search for catharsis.<\/span><\/p>\n<h3>Post-show talk<\/h3>\n<p><strong>12 November: <\/strong>Following the performance, writer and broadcaster Peter Curran (<em>Bunk Bed<\/em> and <em>No Blacks No Irish<\/em> on BBC Radio 4) will host a brief Q&amp;A with Johnny Daukes, exploring some of the themes raised by <em>SQUID \u2013 <\/em>memory, abuse, creativity and the strange ways in which art can reveal things before we\u2019re ready to understand them.<\/p>\n","dates":["2026-11-11","2026-11-12","2026-11-13","2026-11-14","2026-11-14"],"date":"2026-11-11 19:00:00","daterange":{"start":"2026-11-11","end":"2026-11-14"},"type":[],"offer":[],"access":[]},{"id":"the-ugly-one","s":"The Ugly One  <p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">\u201cDoes a flawless face exist?\u201d<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Lette has everything: a successful career, a loving wife, and a brilliant invention. Then he discovers the one thing nobody dared tell him \u2014 he\u2019s hideous. A radical operation to \u201cresculpture the entire facial area\u201d leads to consequences far beyond what he, or anyone else, could possibly imagine.\u00a0<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Following the acclaimed run of <\/span><i><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">An Ideal Husband<\/span><\/i><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">, Broken Nose Theatre presents Marius von Mayenburg\u2019s iconic black comedy <\/span><i><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">The Ugly One<\/span><\/i><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">, directed by Ramin Gray. Twenty years after premiering <\/span><i><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">The Ugly One<\/span><\/i><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> at the Royal Court, Gray returns to Mayenburg\u2019s play in a world that has fulfilled its prophecy.<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">A razor-sharp satire about beauty, identity and self-love.<\/span><\/p>\n","dates":["2026-11-17","2026-11-18","2026-11-19","2026-11-20","2026-11-21","2026-11-21","2026-11-23","2026-11-24","2026-11-25","2026-11-26","2026-11-27","2026-11-28","2026-11-28","2026-11-30","2026-12-01","2026-12-02","2026-12-03","2026-12-04","2026-12-05","2026-12-05","2026-12-07","2026-12-08","2026-12-09","2026-12-10","2026-12-11","2026-12-12","2026-12-12","2026-12-14","2026-12-15","2026-12-16","2026-12-17","2026-12-18","2026-12-19","2026-12-19"],"date":"2026-11-17 19:00:00","daterange":{"start":"2026-11-17","end":"2026-12-19"},"type":[],"offer":[],"access":[]},{"id":"incident-at-vichy","s":"Incident at Vichy  <p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">A rare revival of one of <\/span><b>Arthur Miller<\/b><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">\u2019s most unflinching and urgent plays.<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">France. 1942. A group of people are detained. Picked up off the street without explanation, they cling to the hope that this is nothing more than a routine identity check.\u00a0<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Over the course of an hour, as one by one they are called away for questioning, a terrible truth begins to emerge: they have been selected not at random, but for who they are.\u00a0<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Rarely performed, <\/span><i><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Incident at Vichy<\/span><\/i><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> confronts our complicity and responsibility in the face of injustice. Olivier and Tony Award-nominated director <strong>Melly Still<\/strong> (<em>Coram Boy,<\/em>\u00a0<em>My Brilliant Friend, Morning &#8217;til Midnight, Revenger&#8217;s Tragedy<\/em>: National Theatre) returns to Arcola following her sold-out production of <em>Sputnik Sweetheart<\/em>. <\/span><\/p>\n","dates":["2027-01-15","2027-01-16","2027-01-18","2027-01-19","2027-01-20","2027-01-21","2027-01-22","2027-01-23","2027-01-23","2027-01-25","2027-01-26","2027-01-27","2027-01-28","2027-01-29","2027-01-30","2027-01-30","2027-02-01","2027-02-02","2027-02-03","2027-02-04","2027-02-04","2027-02-05","2027-02-06","2027-02-06","2027-02-08","2027-02-09","2027-02-10","2027-02-11","2027-02-11","2027-02-12","2027-02-13","2027-02-13","2027-02-15","2027-02-16","2027-02-17","2027-02-18","2027-02-18","2027-02-19","2027-02-20","2027-02-20"],"date":"2027-01-15 19:00:00","daterange":{"start":"2027-01-15","end":"2027-02-20"},"type":[],"offer":[],"access":["captioned-performance","relaxed-performance"]},{"id":"the-reckoning-2027","s":"The Reckoning  <p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">A journalist meets a man in a ruined village outside Kyiv.<\/span><\/p>\n<p><i><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Why don&#8217;t you start with when the war began for you?<\/span><\/i><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">The Man from Stoyanka is a security guard, just an ordinary man. But when everyone else flees, he stays. As his home turns into a no man&#8217;s land, he chooses to take extraordinary action.<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">And she&#8217;s there to record it &#8211; for the history books, for the courts, for humanity.<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Playful and unsettling, Offie-nominated <\/span><i><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">The Reckoning<\/span><\/i><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> is a vivid and powerful new play about war, survival and the fragile trust between those who uncover the truth and those who must live with it.<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Based on real events within The Reckoning Project&#8217;s verified archive of witness testimonies of the Russian war in Ukraine, each performance is followed by Food for Thought, a reflection from a journalist, lawyer or those with direct experience of the conflict.<\/span><\/p>\n","dates":["2027-02-17","2027-02-18","2027-02-19","2027-02-20","2027-02-20","2027-02-22","2027-02-23","2027-02-24","2027-02-25","2027-02-26","2027-02-27","2027-02-27"],"date":"2027-02-17 19:00:00","daterange":{"start":"2027-02-17","end":"2027-02-27"},"type":[],"offer":[],"access":[]}]
            </script>
            					</div>
				
				
				

